course: dictionary
lesson: 5874
title: Manga: comics from Japan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A manga is a comic from Japan. Many manga are graphic novels, which means they tell a long story with pictures and speech bubbles. The context gives you clues: «Anime and manga have their own style with big eyes and simple noses» tells you that manga has a special way of drawing.
explain: Manga are usually read from right to left, the opposite of most English books. Start at the top right corner of the page and work across and down. If a story seems to jump around, you may be reading it the wrong way.
explain: The word also means a drawing style, with big eyes, simple noses and speed lines that show movement. You can talk about a «manga-style drawing» when you copy this look in art. Some manga are for adults, so check the age rating before you read one.
fact: Manga are Japanese comics and graphic novels.
fact: Manga are usually read from right to left.
fact: Manga has a special drawing style, with big eyes and speed lines.
fact: Many manga become anime, which are Japanese cartoons.
fact: Many libraries have a manga section, and some manga are for adults, so always check the age rating.
exercise: What is manga? | Japanese food served in small bowls | A type of English poem | A kind of music played on drums | *Japanese comics and graphic novels
exercise: Which way are most manga usually read? | From left to right | From top to bottom only | From the back page to the front | *From right to left
exercise: Your friend wants to read a manga for adults. What should you check first? | The colour of the cover | The name of the artist | *The age rating | The number of pages
test: What does «manga-style drawing» mean? | *Drawing in the style of Japanese comics, with big eyes and speed lines | Drawing with only one colour | Drawing very large animals | Drawing a map of a city
test: What is an anime? | *A Japanese cartoon, often based on a manga | A Japanese snack | A kind of English comic | A library card
exam: Maya says manga is just like English comics and is read from left to right. What is the correct answer? | Manga has no pictures at all | Manga is only for very young children | *Manga is usually read from right to left, so Maya is wrong | Manga is read from left to right, like all books
